      "claim": "In the closest transferable human context, procainamide (para-substituted benzamide with a basic aminoethyl amide) has absolute oral bioavailability values of approximately 65-95% across conventional and sustained-release formulations, all above the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C03", "C17", "C26", "C32", "C37", "C38", "C40", "C67", "C77"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for procainamide and NAPA show measurable steady-state oral AUC and Cmax in humans (procainamide AUC 9.88 mg·h/L, Cmax 2.07 mg/L; NAPA AUC 9.85 mg·h/L), confirming meaningful oral systemic exposure; cimetidine coadministration increased procainamide AUC to 14.12 mg·h/L (~43%), indicating some first-pass/clearance component but not low F.",
      "card_ids": ["C104", "C128", "C92", "C121"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "A close moclobemide-like analog (M05) reached Cmax at about 1.4 h in humans with normal and impaired renal function, indicating rapid oral absorption; this supports but does not directly quantify F.",
      "card_ids": ["C125", "C132"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only low absolute F value in the closest context is 7.2% in domestic pigs (C71), attributed to species-specific first-pass hepatic extraction; it is not transferable as affirmative evidence for F < 20% in the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C71"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C125", "C132", "C104", "C128", "C92", "C121"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule under fed conditions was supplied.",
    "No query-specific food-effect data; the fed-state condition is inferred only from structurally related compounds.",
    "The closest L3 analog (M05) differs from the query by a morpholinone rather than morpholine ring, and only Tmax data are available for it.",
    "Procainamide differs from the query at the para substituent (NH2 vs Cl) and the basic amine (diethylamino vs morpholino), so first-pass and transport behavior may differ.",
    "The only low-F procainamide value is from pigs (C71), and no affirmative human evidence supports F < 20% for the query or its close analogs."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high: the closest transferable human context (procainamide) consistently shows absolute oral bioavailability of about 65-95%, L3 exposure records confirm meaningful oral systemic exposure and rapid absorption for close analogs, the physicochemical prior is favorable, and the only low F value is pig-specific and not transferable; no affirmative evidence supports F < 20%."
}

